 level, reported food intake, smoking habits and area of living</article-title><source>Public Health Nutr</source><year>2001</year><fpage>919</fpage><lpage>927</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11527517</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Johansson</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Hallmans</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Wikman</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Biessy</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Riboli</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaaks</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Validation and Calibration of food-frequency questionnaire in the Northern Sweden Health and Disease Cohort</article-title><source>Public Health Nutr</source><year>2002</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>487</fpage><lpage>496</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12003662</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1079/PHN2001315</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Livingstone</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name><name><surname>Black</surname><given-names>AE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Markers of the validity of reported energy intake</article-title><source>J Nutr</source><year>2003</year><volume>133</volume><fpage>895S</fpage><lpage>920S</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12612176</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Smedman</surname><given-names>AE</given-names></name><name><surname>Gustafsson</surname><given-names>IB</given-names></name><name><surname>Berglund</surname><given-names>LG</given-names></name><name><surname>Vessby</surname><given-names>BO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pentadecanoic acid in serum as a marker for intake of milk fat: relations between intake of milk fat and metabolic risk factors</article-title><source>Am J Clin Nutr</source><year>1999</year><volume>69</volume><fpage>22</fpage><lpage>29</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9925119</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wennberg</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Vessby</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Johansson</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evaluation of relative intake of fatty acids according to the Northern Sweden FFQ with fatty acid level in erythrocyte membranes as biomarkers</article-title><source>Public Health Nutr</source><year>2009</year><comment></comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19144238</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wolk</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Furuheim</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Vessby</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Fatty acid composition of adipose tissue and serum lipids are valid biological markers of dairy fat intake in men</article-title><source>J Nutr</source><year>2001</year><volume>131</volume><fpage>828</fpage><lpage>833</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11238766</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wolk</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Vessby</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Ljung</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Barrefors</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evaluation of a biological marker of dairy fat intake</article-title><source>Am J Clin Nutr</source><year>1998</year><volume>68</volu